  I have put the latest PC-Nethack v3.0 at patchlevel 6 here at 
lampwick.berkeley.edu.  It is in 2 ZIP files, NH30EXE.ZIP and
NH30SUP.ZIP.  Get them both, unZIP them into a directory, play
with the NETHACK.CNF file to set the directory you put it in,
and run it.  I have found that it is unplayable on a 10 MHz XT-clone,
barely playable on a PS/2 model 30-286, but quite playable on a
16 MHz 386 machine.  A fast hard disk is probably necessary, as
the overlays use the drive a lot.  If you have a lot of memory, it
will probably be worth it to stick the main executable in a RAMdrive,
or at least use a big disk cache.

  Also on lampwick is the complete Nethack 3.0 PL 6 source tree in
Zoo format.  

